{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/99154-the-coup-o-noodles-and-the-storm-scenario-all-the-apocalypses-at-once","id":99154,"title":"The Coup O Noodles and the Storm Scenario: ALL THE APOCALYPSES AT ONCE!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-26T07:33:55-07:00","id":99154,"title":"The Coup O Noodles and the Storm Scenario: ALL THE APOCALYPSES AT ONCE!","content":"So...i know some do Crossovers (i love them) But.. concidering that on crossover sense, the OWoD is a coup of noodles fill with every sort of weird creature...and the storm being the apocalypse,gehhena,reckoning, armaggedon etc....<br /> <br /> How do you run them all at the same time?<br /> <br /> Theres some which are easier to pull like wraith since it was the earliest. but How to deal With Tzimitsce going Godzilla on NY, Belial pulling a cthulhu god like thing, the technocratic union fighting pretty much everything while running in circles and shouting &quot;DONT PANIC! EVERYTHING IS UNDER CONTROL.&quot; while millions of god like what horrors of the umbra roll into reality...and the hunters well....erm..being hunters...oh and The Wyrm eating pittsburg","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T12:27:06-07:00","id":99403,"title":"","content":"I've had something similar happen. The game ended in 8 simultaneous Apocalypses, most of them directly caused by the PCs. I posted about this in another thread, but I'll repost what I remember here. This was years ago so I may be wrong on some details but here is what I remember.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That game was absolutely nuts. It actually ended in 8 simultaneous apocalypses, 5 of them directly caused by the PCs. This was about 4 years ago, so I think I'm remembering most of this right, but I could be missing or misremembering some things. If any of my former players are on here and see this, feel free to correct any mistakes.<br /> <br /> It started as an elders game in Dark Ages and I just kept going to the point of ludicrousness to see how long I could hold on. Most of the game played like a protracted game of Vampire Civ, adjudicating large sweeping decisions that affected world politics as the players played elder chess with each other manipulating minions and really pulling the strings of the Jyhad brilliantly. By the time we hit modern nights, the whole group was 4th gen (many diableries) and had over 2500 xp a piece. It was nuts.<br /> <br /> As they affected history as they went, world canon changed quite a bit. The two Justicar seats that were held were Lasombra and Setite (the Baali was infiltrating the Setites and managed to pull off convincing the elders in Memphis to let him take a faction of Setites to the Camarilla to work to corrupt them from within). <br /> <br /> By the time I was getting a bit done with the game (it had been going on for about 18 months at this point) I started rumblings of a Gehenna plot, figuring it would be interesting to play through Gehenna from the side of the Elders and end this game with a bang. In response to the rumblings of Gehenna that are proving more than just rumors, each side runs to their respective cross-sphere allies.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra had close ties with several groups of mages and immortals (highlander style, I incorporate them into WoD as per the homebrew supplement). He was one who forcibly got his Quickening stripped by a mage before he was embraced. Through work with them he manages to reawaken his Quickening and become the One by defeating the only other survivor who was a Marauder Archmage champion on top of his Quickening 10 in a decidedly unfair duel, the power of which he channeled to rip massive holes in the Gauntlet and break much of causal reality, thus breaking Paradox and allowing the Archmages to return from Horizon. He planned to use the combined force of an army of Archmages all of whom were channeling the raw power of God himself (the Abyss that he linked them to through a homebrew level 9 Abyss Mysticism ritual) to amplify the natural power over fate he got as The One to rewrite reality to offset Gehenna. <br /> <br /> In the meantime the Baali had been rather successfully playing both Gaian werewolves and Black Spiral Dancers off against each other while maintaining strong alliances with both. He also had strong alliances to several very powerful Earthbound Demons. Somehow (Presence 9 had a good deal to do with it) he manages to get the Gaian werewolves and Black Spiral Dancers all so confused that they are actually working together to summon the Wyrm into the material world in a forbidden rite that he is combining with his own use of Call the Great Beast, along with a level 9 Dark Thaumaturgy ritual meant to merge the two of them together in a massive power overload of sheer evil. He then combined this with a massive ritual performed worldwide by the cults of 3 of the Archdukes of Hell to funnel all of the Faith inherent in the Garou people in their Triat into this monstrosity (completely neutralizing the werewolves in the process) and supercharging this nightmare even more. <br /> <br /> By this point I'm just sitting back and watching them work. The world is definitely ending at this point. It's just a question of who gets there first. I look at the Gehenna book and it is clearly insufficient to cover this nightmare so I wing it. Saulot comes back, having ALLIED with Tremere (I pulled an unexpected and set it up that all of this was a joint plan of the two of them all along). Working with them is Haqim who pulls in Brujah (not Troile, notably), Ravnos, Lasombra and Cappadocius all on one side. Opposing them is an alliance of Ennoia, Arikel, Absimiliard, Malkav (who can't stand how much his brother has been corrupted as he sees it by this plan with Tremere), Augustus Giovanni, Ventrue, Tzimisce and Set. They set up for their grand war that will swallow the earth, but wake up to find 2 other players in the game in the massive constructs of stupid power in the form of the monstrosity of evil created by the Baali and the army of Archmages channeling God created by the Lasombra. <br /> <br /> At this point God has had enough with this shit and the Angels return to scour the earth with heavenly fire. I wasn't going to run that combat. Not on your life.<br /> <br /> I think I'm missing a few as I am confident on the 8 apocalypses, but I think that was the gist. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T12:31:06-07:00","id":99409,"title":"","content":"You pretty much answered your own question. All that stuff happens at once. It's basically the craziest, most over-the-top Roland Emmerich movie EVER. I would also like to add that you forgot about the antediluvians running around willy nilly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:36:30-07:00","id":99657,"title":"","content":"I don't mind crossovers, particularly if the Player Characters are from one gameline. There is no real issue that messes with Werewolf Cosmology to have say the Pack figuring out how to stop an Antediluvian or something.<br /> <br /> And its the Apocalypse... its allowed to be crazytownbananapants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:48:25-07:00","id":99667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/99154-the-coup-o-noodles-and-the-storm-scenario-all-the-apocalypses-at-once?p=99657#post99657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And its the Apocalypse... its allowed to be crazytownbananapants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah if the world's gonna end, for good or bad it better go out in one damn big bang.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T19:26:25-07:00","id":103068,"title":"","content":"I still need to read all of the Time of Judgement, and Ascension, but I read Gehenna and Apocalypse. It seemed to me they included on Scenario that was Everything happens, that could tie in with the other books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T18:23:41-07:00","id":103755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/99154-the-coup-o-noodles-and-the-storm-scenario-all-the-apocalypses-at-once?p=103068#post103068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still need to read all of the Time of Judgement, and Ascension, but I read Gehenna and Apocalypse. It seemed to me they included on Scenario that was Everything happens, that could tie in with the other books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ascension's worth getting, Time of Judgment on the other hand is the weakest of the line end books, namely because they cram in CtD, KotE, HtR, DtF and MtR together, leading them to really skimp on all of them. Like the HtR chapter, the opening section is truly awesome with newspaper clips of disasters and growing signs of the ToJ, posts on the Hunter.net, and some letters written by prominent Hunters, ending with a cryptic message from Witness1. The next section about the build up to the ToJ for Hunters is good unfortunately the rest is largely generic and uninspiring. Honestly their stuff feels more like [insert other gameline]'s apocalypse is happening and the Imbued are just along for the ride. Admittedly that is kind of what they were meant to be but it just feels cheap. Similarly other Chapters have interesting scenarios but many of them feel rushed and/or bare-boned.<br /> <br /> Honestly if you don't have the book already I wouldn't get it unless you can get it cheap or it's a part of one of DriveThruRPG's gameline bundles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-01T19:02:20-07:00","id":103769,"title":"","content":"I already have both books but I got them late after I read the three novels and Gehenna and Apocalypse. I was in the middle of reading Exalted's gameline when I got them, and I never fit them in the schedule. I remember being Underwhelmed by the Portrayal of Angels. But the Shih boost seemed really cool in the Middle Kingdom Section. And I didn't read any of the Ascension.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}